The paramagnetic coupling term for a hydrogen atom in a magnetic field is of order

\[
\langle H\rangle \sim m\mu_B B
\]

For small \(m\), take \(m\sim 1\). With \(B=1\,\text{T}\),

\[
\mu_B B \approx 9.27\times 10^{-24}\,\text{J}
\approx 5.79\times 10^{-5}\,\text{eV}
\]

The transition energy for \(\lambda = 0.4861\,\mu\text{m} = 486.1\,\text{nm}\) is

\[
\Delta E = \frac{hc}{\lambda}
\approx \frac{1240\,\text{eV}\cdot\text{nm}}{486.1\,\text{nm}}
\approx 2.55\,\text{eV}
\]

Thus,

\[
\langle H\rangle \sim 10^{-5}\,\text{eV} \ll \Delta E \sim 1\,\text{eV}
\]

